KORTEX PAST EXAMINATION PAPERS
LAW - Law of Torts (Year 2024)

Q1. The landmark case Donoghue v Stevenson (1932) established which doctrine?
  (A) The Neighbour Principle and Duty of Care
  (B) Strict liability in wild animal custody
  (C) Sovereign immunity
  (D) Res ipsa loquitur in surgery
  Answer: A - Donoghue v Stevenson formulated the Neighbour Principle in negligence law.


